ages/eb/eb114471d69ebd728a176b521ab410ab2b16d2bccc039e003faacd9c5d445e96.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $\\color{blue}5$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 3 4 \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{3}{20}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142945 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9de1ed1f-02ca-52bd-81ae-7315ecb6048d" "question-5bd2d1e1-68de-57c1-bff5-68ec9a1e6a06" "question-c2a77996-340d-501b-8df6-d80bcca2d5c2" "question-7075490b-ba39-590b-9bf6-e2f4c266c36e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142720 :question/problem "Use the model below to calculate $\\dfrac{5}{6} \\div 4.$\n\n![](images/d1/d1c1c3842b04174137bfe8a938c70493493b2c9a0e74bee619d965446c9326a6.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to divide by $\\color{blue}4$, we split the whole into $\\color{blue}4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/24/24bffed596b77ba53d57e04ebb6baede437d40f825c03a794ae7689f11c3c250.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{5}{24}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{6} \\div 4 = \\dfrac{5}{24} \\, .\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-74253b72-bcb5-5e5c-81f4-dbdc4d66711f" :question/id #uuid "74253b72-bcb5-5e5c-81f4-dbdc4d66711f" :question/math-academy-id "q-61153" :question/problem "![](images/87/87d71379739f4abfe7f47f31448f5245bdfba8d6986d5746a3deb67f49acabef.png)\n\nWhat division problem is represented by the model above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{1}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{1}{15}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/ba/bafb6b86ebc3c330d202cb340c7d7a5fbea2982e689bc9e8c8cbce74e50d49fe.png)\n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}÷3=\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :q