m shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷4=\\frac{2}{12}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186142221 :answer-field/correct 17592186142223 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-175f029d-3a5f-53c9-899b-6473231cb987" :question/id #uuid "175f029d-3a5f-53c9-899b-6473231cb987" :question/math-academy-id "q-61231" :question/problem "![](images/17/177011333d5e29ed699884a665aa58aea43eec52b64d045daa5370a71e9f2a96.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the division problem above?" :question/worked-solution "We have $\\frac{4}{7}$ on the left and $\\frac{4}{14}$ on the right.\n\n![](images/9a/9a2f2136b843a54c3038b2905570d1932b2547279953093f3b6c89fc65d4b11b.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $2$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right.  \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}÷2=\\frac{4}{14}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38a44da7-0543-5023-aea9-074c4f6b3e92"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38a44da7-0543-5023-aea9-074c4f6b3e92" :answer-field/id #uuid "38a44da7-0543-5023-aea9-074c4f6b3e92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3e4adc2c-1985-5645-bb66-c0a09ee8de75" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3e4adc2c-1985-5645-bb66-c0a09ee8de75" "answer-cc5e07f2-a4f4-5eda-acd7-5f8f3c974d14" "answer-805979da-0872-5d4a-a69d-a023ca171302" "answer-8e883dad-7c79-57fe-9969-050966ee92b7" "answer-733ce884-d9fa-57ea-b302-23a3a4fcc7ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3e4adc2c-1985-5645-bb66-c0a09ee8de75" :answer/id #uuid "3e4adc2c-1985-5645-bb66-c0a09ee8de75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc5e07f2-a4f4-5eda-acd7-5f8f