 divide by $3$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/fe/fe13a38598359a92be567c1a4c3b1e0fb1c4d8c3ed6522dda37171c1ff5f2668.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{2}{15}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}÷3=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e46a352d-d27e-53e3-8248-0f6a8c22b01b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e46a352d-d27e-53e3-8248-0f6a8c22b01b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e46a352d-d27e-53e3-8248-0f6a8c22b01b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2b60e537-cf9d-52fb-83b3-0bac78e47dda" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b60e537-cf9d-52fb-83b3-0bac78e47dda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b60e537-cf9d-52fb-83b3-0bac78e47dda" :answer/id #uuid "2b60e537-cf9d-52fb-83b3-0bac78e47dda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7075490b-ba39-590b-9bf6-e2f4c266c36e" :question/id #uuid "7075490b-ba39-590b-9bf6-e2f4c266c36e" :question/math-academy-id "q-100611" :question/problem "![](images/94/94c0b0551d2f7ec745b30d8edd08a45257f6f3daf581798ee97b82ba277e5fee.png)\n\nUse the model above to calculate $\\frac{3}{4}÷5.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we need to divide by $5$, we split the whole into $5$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](images/6f/6f6f8eda89ca98c62fe583fc6218f497bdf1a7056b792ade26edd064ffba2c95.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{3}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}÷5=\\frac{3}{20}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f06d672-38d4-5fe4-a2e8-52e19971d84c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f06d672-38d4-5fe4-a2e8-52e19971d84c" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f06d672-38d4-5fe4-a2e8-52e19971d84c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-58e888a1-b6d6-569e-aa2d-f4a6e4fa5c62" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06f9c877-3cd5-54ff-b304-3d5e30059ffa" "answer-58e888a1-b6d6-569e-aa2d-f4a6e4fa5c62" "answer-b4db9a7a-1f7c-5f71-ab3b-e8f3e5618c49" "answer-81c46354-3263-564a-b0e9-6369b61bf031" "answer-dd1252b9-adba-5a42-b13c-aedc82858cb1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06f9c877-3cd5-54ff-b304-3d5e30059ffa" :answer/id #uuid "06f9c877-3cd5-54ff-b304-3d5e30059ffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58e888a1-b6d6-569e-aa2d-f4a6e4fa5c62" :answer/id #uuid "58e888a1-b6d6-569e-aa2d-f4a6e4fa5c62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4db9a7a-1f7c-5f71-ab3b-e8f3e5618c49" :answer/id #uuid "b4db9a7a-1f7c-5f71-ab3b-e8f3e5618c49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81c46354-3263-564a-b0e9-6369b61bf031" :answer/id #uuid "81c46354-3263-564a-b0e9-6369b61bf031" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd1252b9-adba-5a42-b13c-aedc82858cb1" :answer/id #uuid "dd1252b9-adba-5a42-b13c-aedc82858cb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144002 :tutorial/content "When we divide a fraction by a whole number, say ${\\color{red}{2}},$ the idea is to \n\n- split the fraction into ${\\color{red}{2}}$ equal parts, and\n\n- determine the fraction that makes up each part.\n\nFor example, suppose we wish to find the value of \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{5} \\div 2.\n$$\n\nLet's start by drawing the fraction model for $\\dfrac45\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/d1/d159ff7e61ae308f27dd561cc8b219f0fc5b5fa46135ebff70ed15558186280b.png)\n\nWe need to divide this fraction by ${\\color{red}{2}}.$ To do this, we draw a horizontal line through our fraction that splits it into $\\color{red}2$ *equal parts*.\n\n![](images/87/87c0a9dad9ab63de7858e8857e412b4d6ce849dfc0b02a172a5debe420c5baf6.png)\n\nWe only need to determine the fraction that makes up one of the parts. Therefore, we can focus on only one row (i.e., the bottom row).\n\nNow, we remove all the shaded parts not in the bottom row. \n\n![](images/54/54a3760d69e7622afa800e4fe107cdafc7069a1fd31138a9ad6c63e8cf6f8f1f.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{4}{10}$ of the whole. Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4}{5} \\div 2 = \\dfrac{4}{10} \\, .\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186143062 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
